ndings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the exact translation from harness RunResult.abstain_reason (parse_error for signal-death, other for raise/no-result, timeout for hang) into the plan's two-part reason/reason_detail, acknowledging that a native crash and a controlled bad-input failure both arrive as parse_error and defining which reason each maps to.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan maps 'invalid/undecodable/unreadable input → parse_error/invalid_input|unreadable_file' AND 'worker crash/protocol failure → other/worker_failure' AND 'deadline → timeout/worker_timeout'.","run_in_worker (harness.py:385-414) maps a signal-death (SIGSEGV/SIGABRT — a hcl2 C-extension crash) to abstain_reason='parse_error', a worker raise or no-result exit to 'other', and a hang to 'timeout'.","The harness therefore emits the SAME parse_error token for a controlled bad-input failure and a hard native crash; the plan wants those on different reason buckets (parse_error vs other/worker_failure) but gives no translation rule from RunResult.abstain_reason to reason/reason_detail."],"finding":"The plan's abstention re-mapping does not specify how the harness's RunResult.abstain_reason values are translated into the plan's two-part reason/reason_detail, and the harness cannot distinguish a controlled bad-input parse failure from a hard C-extension crash — both can surface as parse_error.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f41bbe6202cb41014","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Operations and contracts → 'Closed abstention mapping' and Structural index → 'parses them in grounding.harness.run_in_worker'","norm_id":"nae6ac22405e10c46","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["python-hcl2 segfaults on a malformed/adversarial .tf file: harness returns parse_error, but the plan intends worker crashes to map to other/worker_failure — the receipt would report parse_error/invalid_input, mislabeling a crash as an input defect.","A worker raises a Python exception during parse: harness returns 'other'; the plan's parse_error/invalid_input arm never fires, so 'invalid input' abstentions may in practice surface as other/worker_failure instead."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a mapping table: harness timeout→timeout/worker_timeout; harness parse_error→parse_error/invalid_input (accepting that a rare native crash is bucketed here) OR route it to other/worker_failure explicitly; harness other→other/worker_failure. Reserve parse_error/unreadable_file for read failures detected BEFORE the worker (byte-capture stage), which the harness never sees.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the exact `reason_detail` token for each of the six `ambiguous` triggers (e.g. duplicate_address, no_unique_address, dynamic_source, computed_value, provider_attribute, splat_index, unknown_tfvars) so the closed receipt schema and the exact-assertion boundary tests are fully specified.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'duplicate/no unique address, dynamic source/expression, computed value, provider attribute, splat/index traversal, or unknown tfvars selection → `ambiguous/<matching_detail>`'","All other rows give concrete tokens (e.g. `no_tool/missing_extra`, `parse_error/invalid_input|unreadable_file`, `other/module_limit|file_limit|byte_limit`); only the ambiguous row uses a placeholder","Plan requires 'its receipt against this closed schema' with 'Terraform reason_detail' as a required field; search_files confirms `reason_detail` is a NEW vocabulary with no prior definition in the repo","AC-5: 'assert every trigger's exact reason/reason_detail' — un-enumerated tokens make the oracle unspecified"],"finding":"The closed abstention mapping fixes an exact reason_detail token for every trigger except the `ambiguous` class, which is left as the placeholder `ambiguous/<matching_detail>`; the exact detail token for each of the six ambiguity triggers (duplicate/no-unique address, dynamic source/expression, computed value, provider attribute, splat/index traversal, unknown tfvars selection) is never defined, though the receipt schema is required to be closed and an AC demands tests assert every trigger's exact reason_detail.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f948c2097f39fbdfe","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Operations and contracts → 'Closed abstention mapping' bullet; AC-5 ('Boundary tests assert every trigger's exact reason/reason_detail')","norm_id":"nfe53305553a62591","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor must emit reason_detail for a duplicate address or a splat traversal but has no canonical token to write","The closed receipt schema's reason_detail enum cannot be authored because the ambiguous member tokens are unknown","Two implementers pick divergent tokens (e.g. `dynamic_source` vs `dynamic_expression`), breaking Pass-2 receipt validation and the exact-match tests"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace `ambiguous/<matching_detail>` with the explicit pairs, e.g.: `ambiguous/duplicate_address`, `ambiguous/no_unique_address`, `ambiguous/dynamic_source`, `ambiguous/computed_value`, `ambiguous/provider_attribute`, `ambiguous/splat_index`, `ambiguous/unknown_tfvars`, and list these as the closed reason_detail enum in terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the exact `terraform_kind` token strings for all declaration classes (e.g. variable, local, output, module, provider, managed_resource, data_resource) so the evidence extension is a closed, exactly-testable vocabulary.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'Extension `terraform_kind` carries the declaration class' with no token list","search_files confirms `terraform_kind` is a NEW vocabulary absent from the repo","AC-3 requires validating 'exact `symbol` mapping'; without fixed tokens (e.g. `managed_resource` vs `resource`, `data_resource` vs `data`) the mapping is not exactly testable"],"finding":"The `terraform_kind` evidence extension is said to 'carry the declaration class' and the seven classes are named only narratively (variables, locals, outputs, modules, providers, managed resources, data resources); the exact token strings are never fixed, yet ACs require 'exact symbol mapping' and receipt/evidence validation against a closed contract.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f777d510761e3e59f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Operations and contracts → 'Extension terraform_kind carries the declaration class'; AC-3/AC-4","norm_id":"neb4411aecc534314","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A lookup_declaration on a managed resource must set terraform_kind but the token (`resource` vs `managed_resource`) is unspecified","Pass-2 receipt validation drifts because Pass-1 and Pass-2 implementers choose different declaration-class tokens"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_i